 "discussion": "SYNOPSIS\n\nA strong low-pressure system moving north off the BC coast will spread cloud and bands of light snow across the area today. Snowfall amounts of 1 to 3 cm are expected, mainly during the morning hours. Tonight and Wednesday, a strengthening southwesterly flow aloft will bring milder temperatures and limit precipitation to just a chance of a brief flurry or two. Winds will be generally light to moderate southeasterly with some gustiness in the alpine. Temperatures will climb slowly through the period.\n\nEXTENDED OUTLOOK\n\nThursday to Saturday: Another disturbance is forecast to move into the southern interior from the coast late Wednesday into Thursday morning, bringing the possibility of a few more cms of snow to the upper slopes. A break in precipitation with partly cloudy skies and cooler temperatures is expected on Friday and Saturday as a weak ridge of high pressure builds over the southern interior.",
